          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.48,
          "end": 38.59,
          "en": "as you have for your Firebase database, just as a side note.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.59,
          "end": 40.47,
          "en": "But here, I will use the same one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.47,
          "end": 42.05,
          "en": "and I will click on hosting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.05,
          "end": 44.7,
          "en": "and you'll find instructions here, but in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.7,
          "end": 47.3,
          "en": "hosting is really simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.3,
          "end": 50.17,
          "en": "If you click on, get started, we see that we first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.17,
          "end": 53.21,
          "en": "need to install an extra tool, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.21,
          "end": 54.57,
          "en": "So let's do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.57,
          "end": 58.24,
          "en": "Let's run this command on Linux and Mac iOS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.24,
          "end": 60.95,
          "en": "you might need to add pseudo in front of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.95,
          "end": 63.78,
          "en": "on Windows You don't need to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.78,
          "end": 68.12,
          "en": "To run this command, and this will then install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.12,
          "end": 72.92,
          "en": "extra tool provided by Firebase globally on your machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.92,
          "end": 77.36,
          "en": "and we'll need that tool to then upload our project later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.36,
          "end": 79.723,
          "en": "So let's wait for this installation to finish.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.58,
          "end": 85.84,
          "en": "And once it is finished, we can go to that next step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.84,
          "end": 89.813,
          "en": "Now we need to log in by running Firebase login.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.89,
          "end": 94.75999999999999,
          "en": "So let's run this and this should open up a tab",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.75999999999999,
          "end": 97.3,
          "en": "in the browser and allow you to log in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.3,
          "end": 99.07,
          "en": "if you're not logged in already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.07,
          "end": 102.52000000000001,
          "en": "or it prompts you for password and your username,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.52000000000001,
          "end": 103.50999999999999,
          "en": "your email address,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.50999999999999,
          "end": 106.11,
          "en": "and you have to log in with those credentials,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.11,
          "end": 109.31,
          "en": "which you used for logging in into your Firebase account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.31,
          "end": 110.68299999999999,
          "en": "before as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.81,
          "end": 115.14,
          "en": "Once that is done, you need to run Firebase in it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.14,
          "end": 118.75,
          "en": "So copy that command, and now in your project folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.75,
          "end": 121.14,
          "en": "in your entire project folder, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.14,
          "end": 123.303,
          "en": "you can run Firebase in it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.39,
          "end": 126.59,
          "en": "And this will ask you a couple of questions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.64,
          "end": 131.77,
          "en": "It asks you which part of Firebase you wanna manage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.77,
          "end": 136.32,
          "en": "with this command line interface, where using at the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.32,
          "end": 139,
          "en": "And we really only want to use hosting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139,
          "end": 141.64,
          "en": "So select hosting with the arrow keys,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.64,
          "end": 146.223,
          "en": "and press space to market, and then enter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.52,
          "end": 150.03,
          "en": "Now, then you're prompted wherever you wanna host this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.03,
          "end": 153.6,
          "en": "into an existing Firebase project or create a new one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.6,
          "end": 155.65,
          "en": "As I said, you could create a new one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.65,
          "end": 157.433,
          "en": "but I will use an existing one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.42000000000002,
          "end": 161.4,
          "en": "And then it should list all the projects you have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.4,
          "end": 163.96,
          "en": "And I'm simply picking that project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.96,
          "end": 166.163,
          "en": "with which I worked early already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.57,
          "end": 169.54,
          "en": "Now we have the interesting part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.54,
          "end": 173.69,
          "en": "It asks us what our public directory should be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 173.69,
          "end": 176.98,
          "en": "And that's important because that's the directory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 176.98,
          "end": 179.993,
          "en": "which holds the files that will actually be uploaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.21,
          "end": 184.313,
          "en": "So here that would be the dist folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 185.48,
          "end": 187.223,
          "en": "So we should enter dist here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 188.63,
          "end": 192.16,
          "en": "Once you entered dist, hit enter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 192.16,
          "end": 194.31,
          "en": "and you're asked whether this should be configured",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 194.31,
          "end": 199.31,
          "en": "as a single page app and rewrite all URLs to /index.html.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 200.39,
          "end": 203.43,
          "en": "Now that can be confusing, why does this matter?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 203.43,
          "end": 204.393,
          "en": "What's this about?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 205.4,
          "end": 207.34,
          "en": "For a single page applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 207.34,
          "end": 210.29,
          "en": "you have to be careful when it comes to routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 210.29,
          "end": 212.34300000000002,
          "en": "and hosting your app on a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.29,
          "end": 215.59,
          "en": "When a user visits your webpage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.59,
          "end": 220,
          "en": "let's say it's hosted on a domain like \"mypage.com,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 220,
          "end": 224.68,
          "en": "a so-called request is sent to the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.68,
          "end": 228.1,
          "en": "Now let's say that request is not to your main domain,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.1,
          "end": 233.1,
          "en": "but it's \"mypage.com/products\" or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.39,
          "end": 237.95,
          "en": "Now, as I just said, that request hits the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.95,
          "end": 241.3,
          "en": "The server where your static web application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 241.3,
          "end": 244.533,
          "en": "your Vue single page application is hosted at.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 245.41,
          "end": 250.22,
          "en": "Now, this server should actually ignore the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 250.22,
          "end": 251.81,
          "en": "that's part of the request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 251.81,
          "end": 254.39,
          "en": "because if it does not ignore it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.39,
          "end": 259.18,
          "en": "then the server will try to find something on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 259.18,
          "end": 260.7,
          "en": "that matches this request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 260.7,
          "end": 263.7,
          "en": "For example, it looks for a product folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 263.7,
          "end": 267.5,
          "en": "in your hosted files and tries to find an HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.5,
          "end": 269.9,
          "en": "in such a products folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 269.9,
          "end": 272.15,
          "en": "And for our app that would fail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 272.15,
          "end": 275.85,
          "en": "because for our app, the folder structure we deploy is this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 275.85,
          "end": 278.26,
          "en": "We have just one HTML file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 278.26,
          "end": 281.283,
          "en": "In our app, for example, we have a /coach's route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 282.28,
          "end": 285.56,
          "en": "but we have no coaches folder here inside of this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 285.56,
          "end": 289.09000000000003,
          "en": "which is the content that will end up on a server though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 289.09000000000003,
          "end": 292.49,
          "en": "That's why we need to tell the server to ignore the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 292.49,
          "end": 296.7,
          "en": "and instead, always return the index.html file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 296.7,
          "end": 299.75,
          "en": "which then in turn contains the JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 299.75,
          "end": 304.75,
          "en": "off our application where then the Vue router can take over",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 305.01,
          "end": 310.01,
          "en": "and handle this path on the client side, so in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 310.06,
          "end": 312.56,
          "en": "And that's really important, the Vue router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 312.56,
          "end": 314.2,
          "en": "does not run on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 314.2,
          "end": 317.24,
          "en": "And therefore, it can only handle the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 317.24,
          "end": 321.18,
          "en": "which is in a URL, if the server ignores it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 321.18,
          "end": 323.98,
          "en": "That development server was already configured",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 323.98,
          "end": 325.3,
          "en": "to work like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 325.3,
          "end": 328.24,
          "en": "which is why we didn't have to worry about that before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 328.24,
          "end": 331.41,
          "en": "But the web servers, real web servers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 331.41,
          "end": 334.023,
          "en": "typically do not ignore it by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 335.03,
          "end": 337.7,
          "en": "And that's my Firebase is asking us here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 337.7,
          "end": 340.96,
          "en": "if we wanna configure this as a single page app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 340.96,
          "end": 343.94,
          "en": "If we choose yes here, which we should,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 343.94,
          "end": 347.96,
          "en": "then Firebase will ignore all requests on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 347.96,
          "end": 352.96,
          "en": "and as mentioned here, rewrite all URLs to index.html.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 353.32,
          "end": 356.773,
          "en": "So that always index.html is served.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 358.55,
          "end": 360.43,
          "en": "So let's choose yes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 360.43,
          "end": 363.3,
          "en": "And now it's tells us that we already have a index.html file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 363.3,
          "end": 365.56,
          "en": "in this, if it should override this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 365.56,
          "end": 369.673,
          "en": "and here we wanna enter, no, because we wanna keep our file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 370.99,
          "end": 374.14,
          "en": "And now with that we initialized everything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 374.14,
          "end": 375.73,
          "en": "Now to really get deployed this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 375.73,
          "end": 377.71,
          "en": "there's just one change I wanna make.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 377.71,
          "end": 380.75,
          "en": "In the public folder in index.html,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 380.75,
          "end": 385.75,
          "en": "we can edit the index.html file before the project is built.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 386.32,
          "end": 389.08,
          "en": "So any changes you want to make to your project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 389.08,
          "end": 391.64,
          "en": "to your HTML code, and here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 391.64,
          "end": 394.48,
          "en": "should be made here, not in this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 394.48,
          "end": 396.42,
          "en": "You should never touch the code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 396.42,
          "end": 398.65,
          "en": "which is generated in a dist folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 398.65,
          "end": 403.55,
          "en": "Instead, edit your input files and rebuilt the project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 403.55,
          "end": 407.18,
          "en": "if you wanna have a different output here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 407.18,
          "end": 410.15999999999997,
          "en": "And here, for example, I wanna edit the title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 410.15999999999997,
          "end": 415.11,
          "en": "It's actually using a placeholder here, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 415.11,
          "end": 417.94,
          "en": "pulling in the title from somewhere else,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 417.94,
          "end": 421.47,
          "en": "but we can delete this and overwrite this with Find a Coach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 421.47,
          "end": 424.25,
          "en": "for example, which is my title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 424.25,
          "end": 426.16,
          "en": "And now we could also add a meta tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
